WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.421
A headlight lamp sits at one point, yet the light leaves as a parallel beam.

2
00:00:06.421 --> 00:00:11.321
A satellite dish gathers a parallel signal into one point.

3
00:00:11.321 --> 00:00:17.826
In this part we find the shape of such a mirror with a differential equation.

4
00:00:17.826 --> 00:00:21.374
The result is beautiful: it is a parabola.

5
00:00:21.624 --> 00:00:23.972
The source is at the origin.

6
00:00:23.972 --> 00:00:29.087
The tangent to the mirror at a point M meets the x axis at T.

7
00:00:29.087 --> 00:00:35.796
By the law of reflection, the angle of incidence equals the angle of reflection.

8
00:00:35.796 --> 00:00:44.852
Since the reflected ray is parallel to the x axis, triangle O M T is isosceles: the distance O T equals O M,

9
00:00:44.852 --> 00:00:48.542
the square root of x squared plus y squared.

10
00:00:48.792 --> 00:00:54.698
T lies to the left of O, so O T equals y over y prime minus x.

11
00:00:54.698 --> 00:01:05.749
Set this equal to the root and solve for y prime: y prime equals y over x plus the root of x squared plus y squared.

12
00:01:05.749 --> 00:01:14.990
Scaling x and y by the same number leaves the fraction unchanged, so the equation is homogeneous.

13
00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:19.724
Here it is easier to treat x as a function of y.

14
00:01:19.724 --> 00:01:27.759
After x equals v times y we get y times v prime equals the root of one plus v squared.

15
00:01:27.759 --> 00:01:38.222
Separate and integrate: the logarithm of v plus the root of one plus v squared equals the logarithm of y over C.

16
00:01:38.472 --> 00:01:46.330
Exponentiate and replace v by x over y: x plus the root equals y squared over C.

17
00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:50.947
Isolate the root, square, and cancel y squared.

18
00:01:50.947 --> 00:01:55.662
Answer: y squared equals two C x plus C squared.

19
00:01:55.662 --> 00:02:04.502
This is a parabola with focus at the origin, and the mirror is a paraboloid of revolution.

20
00:02:04.752 --> 00:02:09.686
The graph shows two parabolas, with C equal to one and two.

21
00:02:09.686 --> 00:02:13.031
All of them share one focus, the origin.

22
00:02:13.031 --> 00:02:17.463
The parameter C only changes the width of the mirror.

23
00:02:17.463 --> 00:02:25.574
When designing a dish engineers choose this parameter, and the receiver always sits at the focus.

24
00:02:25.824 --> 00:02:32.535
Check question: what type is the equation of the mirror problem?

25
00:02:32.535 --> 00:02:35.366
Decide from its right side.
